# Trading safety (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

- Paper first. `EXECUTION_MODE=paper`, `ENABLE_REAL_TRADING=false`,
  `PROVIDER_MODE=fallback` (staging). `EXCHANGE_MODE` stays non-live: safe default
  `paper_internal` (Mode A); Mode C `paper_exchange_demo` only when explicitly configured;
  Mode D real execution remains disabled. Never weaken these.
- No automatic live orders, withdrawals, transfers, leverage changes, or exchange account
  mutations. `real_trading_enabled` stays false unless a separate task explicitly enables it.
  - **Exception — BloFin DEMO leverage, owner-configured (APPROVED by Sofien on 2026-11-04 — demo only, leverage/margin-mode writes only (automatic close-position NOT approved); PR #430 / `claude/demo-configured-leverage-v3`):**
    the governed demo loop may set margin mode and leverage on the allowlisted BloFin
    **demo host only**, to the value the org owner configured (1–20x, default 10x isolated),
    only when `GOVERNED_DEMO_AUTO_LEVERAGE_WRITE_ENABLED=true` in a staging/local
    environment, on a flat account, with exact read-back, kill-switch re-check and an
    audit record of old/new values. Any non-demo host refuses. No live or production
    leverage change is ever automatic.
- Any sensitive future action requires: explicit human approval, audit logs, idempotency,
  conservative validation, and a kill switch.
- Risk calculations must be deterministic and tested. The risk engine's `BLOCK` is final.
- Market data must carry source + freshness (`is_live`, `fallback_used`). Missing, stale,
  conflicting, or degraded data must trigger conservative behavior.
- Never imply guaranteed returns or autonomous profitability.
- Respect `core/deployment_safety.py` and `core/exchange_safety.py` invariants.

## Broker/exchange operating modes (`.ai/MASTER_WORKFLOW.md` §7)
- **A — none (default):** internal paper portfolio, public market data, mocks, backtests. No
  external account reads/mutations, no live orders.
- **B — read-only:** balances/positions/history/market data only, read-only credentials, no
  withdrawal or trade permission, source+freshness timestamps, graceful degradation.
- **C — paper/demo:** clearly labeled demo, separate credentials, full audit trail, no route to
  production trading.
- **D — real execution:** disabled by default; cannot be enabled by an ordinary implementation
  task — requires a separate, explicitly authorized safety/risk/approval/rollback program.
